# What may enter the build context.
#
# Written as "exclude everything, then re-admit what the build needs", rather
# than as a list of things to keep out. A denylist is only as good as the last
# person to remember to extend it; this way a new top-level file or directory is
# excluded until somebody names it here on purpose.
#
# tests/unit/deployment/test_container_contract.py asserts both halves: that the
# things below stay out, and that everything the Dockerfile COPYs is admitted.

# --- exclude everything ---------------------------------------------------
*

# --- what the image is built from -----------------------------------------
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src
!configs
!.streamlit
!scripts/prepare_demo_bundle.py

# --- and, for Dockerfile.render only, the single-container deployment ------
#
# The VPS image copies none of these; they are admitted so the Render build has
# a supervisor to run as PID 1, a verifier to fail the build on an unverifiable
# bundle, and a proxy configuration it cannot bind-mount because Render has no
# bind mounts. Named individually rather than admitting `scripts/` or `deploy/`
# wholesale, so a future file in either directory is still outside the context
# until somebody names it here.
!scripts/verify_serving_bundle.py
!scripts/render_entrypoint.py
!deploy/render/Caddyfile

# --- and nothing generated, cached, local, or private, even under those ----
#
# The re-admissions above are directories, so their contents come with them.
# These re-exclusions are what keep a stale build tree or a stray cache from
# riding in on `!src` or `!configs`.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~

# Local secrets and Streamlit's secret store. Neither should exist in this
# project -- the service accepts no credential material -- and an image is the
# wrong place to discover that one does.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/secrets.toml

# Scientific outputs. These are produced by the `prepare` service into a named
# volume; an image carrying one would make the image the provenance of a frozen
# decision, which is exactly what the serving bundle contract exists to prevent.
**/*.parquet
**/*.joblib
**/*.pkl
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
